[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/tests/semver_solver_impl_test.py: The suite leaves contracted range and resolution behaviours unexercised, so the required 100% statement coverage is not attainable from the tests: the '==', '!=', '<=' and '>' comparators are never evaluated as satisfaction predicates on full versions; the tilde prefix is never applied to a full semver version such as '~1.2.3'; the caret prefix is never applied to a major-zero wildcard line ('^0.x'), a zero-major triple wildcard ('^0.0.x'), or a zero-major full version ('^0.0.3'), so the first-non-zero-component caret boundary rules are only partly exercised; wildcard normalization omits the bare major wildcard form (a '<major>.x' expression with no relational operator), the '<' and '<=' comparator forms against a wildcard line, the wildcard-in-both-trailing-positions form ('<major>.x.x'), and unbounded wildcard bounds combined with '<', '>' or '!=' which must match no version at all; hyphen ranges are only exercised with a wildcard upper bound and never with two full semver bounds (e.g. '1.0.0 - 2.0.0') whose upper bound is inclusive; precedence comparison never asserts the converse prerelease ranking where an alphanumeric segment outranks a numeric segment; and resolution scenarios in which a candidate release's dependency range contradicts an already-selected release (requiring rejection of that candidate and selection of the highest compatible lower release) and multi-level conflict scenarios that introduce a brand-new transitive package and then restore the accumulated constraints so a lower release remains resolvable are never exercised, leaving the resolution postconditions that every assignment is mutually compatible and that the highest precedence compatible release is selected only partially verified. All of these are explicit postconditions and syntax cases contracted for parse_range, satisfies, compare_precedence, and resolve in the low-level specification and must be covered.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: The trailing 'return None' fallback of the range-bound exclusive upper-bound helper is unreachable under the specification closure: a parsed bound is either fully specified (major, minor, and patch all present) or one of the wildcard forms where the minor component is absent ('<major>.x'), the patch component is absent ('<major>.<minor>.x'), or every component is absent (the unbounded wildcard), because a bound with no major component always carries no minor or patch component; both call sites invoke the helper only after establishing that the bound is not fully specified, so the final fallback can never be taken and no conforming public range expression reaches it. Prune that fallback or annotate it with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: <reason>)' consistent with the sibling upper-bound guard, so that 100% statement coverage is attainable.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/tests/semver_solver_impl_test.py: Resolved coverage feedback: added explicit ==, =, !=, <, <=, >, >= full-version satisfaction predicates; ~1.2.3 full-version tilde; ^0.x, ^0.0.x, ^0.0.3 first-non-zero caret boundaries; bare 1.x wildcard, 1.x.x double-trailing wildcard, <1.x / <=1.x / <=1.2.x comparator wildcards, and unbounded <*, >*, !=* that match no version; 1.0.0 - 2.0.0 inclusive hyphen range; converse prerelease ranking where alphanumeric outranks numeric; Version.format()/__str__ round-trip; and solver scenarios rejecting a candidate whose dependency contradicts an already-selected release, plus a multi-level conflict introducing a new transitive package whose constraints are restored so lower releases resolve. All new syntax forms also exercise parse_range acceptance.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Resolved feedback: pruned the unreachable trailing 'return None' fallback from _RangeBound.high_version by making the helper non-optional (both wildcard upper-bound returns are reachable via '<major>.x' and '<major>.<minor>.x' forms) and simplified both call sites accordingly; also pruned sibling dead guards in the clause compiler and type-checking-only unreachable raises annotated with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: ...)' so statement coverage is attainable.
